@startuml
title ThingsBoard 3.6 Session 与 Device State：OPEN、activity、CLOSED 与 inactivity
skinparam backgroundColor #FFFFFF
skinparam defaultFontName "Microsoft YaHei"
skinparam defaultFontColor #111827
skinparam sequenceArrowColor #1F2937
skinparam sequenceLifeLineBorderColor #374151
skinparam sequenceLifeLineBackgroundColor #FFFFFF
skinparam participantBorderColor #1F2937
skinparam participantBackgroundColor #F8FAFC
skinparam participantFontColor #111827
skinparam actorBorderColor #1F2937
skinparam actorBackgroundColor #EAF7FB
skinparam noteBackgroundColor #FFF7D6
skinparam noteBorderColor #92400E
skinparam noteFontColor #111827
skinparam groupBorderColor #374151
skinparam groupHeaderBackgroundColor #E5E7EB
skinparam groupFontColor #111827
skinparam databaseBorderColor #1F2937
skinparam databaseBackgroundColor #ECFDF5
skinparam collectionsBorderColor #1F2937
skinparam collectionsBackgroundColor #EFF6FF
skinparam ArrowThickness 1.6
skinparam maxMessageSize 230
hide footbox

actor "Device" as Device
participant "Protocol Handler\nMQTT / CoAP / HTTP / LwM2M" as Protocol
participant "DefaultTransportService" as Transport
collections "Transport sessions\nand activity states" as LocalState
queue "Core Queue\ntb_core.<partition>" as CoreQueue
participant "DefaultTbCoreConsumerService" as CoreConsumer
participant "App / Tenant Actors" as ParentActors
participant "DeviceActorMessageProcessor" as DeviceActor
collections "Device Session Cache\nCaffeine / Redis" as SessionCache
participant "DefaultDeviceStateService" as DeviceState
database "SERVER_SCOPE attributes\nor state telemetry" as StateStore
queue "Rule Engine Queue" as RuleQueue
participant "Rule Chain" as RuleChain
queue "Transport notification\nper serviceId" as NotifyQueue

== ASYNC session OPEN ==
Device -> Protocol : network connect or long-lived observation
Protocol -> Protocol : authenticate and create SessionInfoProto
Protocol -> Transport : process(sessionInfo, ASYNC OPEN, callback)
Transport -> Transport : checkLimits()
Transport -> LocalState : onActivity(sessionId, now)
Transport -> Transport : resolve TB_CORE by deviceId hash
Transport -> CoreQueue : ToCoreMsg(toDeviceActorMsg.sessionEvent=OPEN)
alt producer callback succeeds
  CoreQueue --> Transport : broker/provider acknowledgement
  Transport --> Protocol : callback.onSuccess()
  Protocol -> Transport : registerAsyncSession(sessionInfo, listener)
  Transport -> LocalState : sessions.computeIfAbsent(sessionId)
  Protocol --> Device : protocol success, for example MQTT CONNACK
else producer callback fails
  CoreQueue --> Transport : callback error
  Transport --> Protocol : callback.onError(error)
  Protocol --> Device : server unavailable and connection close
end
note over Device,CoreQueue
  Protocol success confirms Queue production only.
  Core consumption and state persistence happen later.
end note

CoreQueue -> CoreConsumer : poll ToCoreMsg pack
CoreConsumer -> ParentActors : TransportToDeviceActorMsgWrapper(callback)
ParentActors -> DeviceActor : route by tenantId and deviceId
DeviceActor -> DeviceActor : processSessionStateMsgs(sessionInfo, OPEN)
alt duplicate sessionId
  DeviceActor -> DeviceActor : ignore duplicate OPEN
else first session for device
  DeviceActor -> DeviceActor : sessions.put(sessionId, metadata)
  DeviceActor -> DeviceState : onDeviceConnect(tenantId, deviceId, now)
  DeviceState -> StateStore : async save lastConnectTime
  DeviceState -> RuleQueue : CONNECT_EVENT
  DeviceActor -> DeviceState : onDeviceActivity(tenantId, deviceId, now)
else additional session
  DeviceActor -> DeviceActor : sessions.put(sessionId, metadata)
  DeviceActor -> DeviceState : onDeviceActivity(tenantId, deviceId, now)
end
DeviceActor -> SessionCache : dump ASYNC session snapshot if cache is non-local
DeviceActor --> ParentActors : callback.onSuccess()
ParentActors --> CoreConsumer : pack callback acknowledged
CoreConsumer -> CoreQueue : commit after pack wait boundary
note over DeviceState,StateStore
  State save is asynchronous. Its callback only logs.
  No transaction spans Actor state, state keys and Rule Engine event.
end note
RuleQueue -> RuleChain : consume CONNECT_EVENT later

== Uplink activity aggregation ==
loop telemetry, attributes, RPC, PING or other accepted uplink
  Device -> Protocol : uplink
  Protocol -> Transport : process(...) or recordActivity(sessionInfo)
  Transport -> LocalState : lastRecordedTime = max(old, now)
end
... default report period 3000 ms ...
Transport -> LocalState : AbstractActivityManager.onReportingPeriodEnd()
LocalState --> Transport : session metadata or previous SessionInfoProto
Transport -> CoreQueue : SubscriptionInfoProto(lastActivityTime, subscriptions)
CoreQueue --> Transport : producer acknowledgement
CoreQueue -> CoreConsumer : poll activity report later
CoreConsumer -> ParentActors : wrapper
ParentActors -> DeviceActor : route by deviceId
DeviceActor -> DeviceActor : handleSessionActivity()
opt Actor still has this session
  DeviceActor -> DeviceActor : refresh last activity and subscription maps
  DeviceActor -> SessionCache : dump updated snapshot for Redis mode
end
DeviceActor -> DeviceState : onDeviceActivity(tenantId, deviceId, reportedTime)
alt reportedTime is newer and state was inactive
  DeviceState -> StateStore : async save lastActivityTime
  DeviceState -> StateStore : async save active=true
  DeviceState -> RuleQueue : ACTIVITY_EVENT
else reportedTime is newer and state already active
  DeviceState -> StateStore : async save lastActivityTime
else stale or non-positive report
  DeviceState -> DeviceState : ignore
end

== Explicit CLOSED and multi-session boundary ==
Device -> Protocol : disconnect or unsubscribe
Protocol -> Transport : process(sessionInfo, ASYNC CLOSED, null)
Protocol -> Transport : deregisterSession(sessionInfo)
Transport -> LocalState : cancel SYNC timer if present and remove listener
Transport -> CoreQueue : ToCoreMsg(sessionEvent=CLOSED)
CoreQueue -> CoreConsumer : poll later
CoreConsumer -> ParentActors : wrapper
ParentActors -> DeviceActor : process CLOSED
DeviceActor -> DeviceActor : remove session and attribute/RPC subscriptions
alt another Actor session remains
  DeviceActor -> SessionCache : dump remaining sessions
else last Actor session closed
  DeviceActor -> DeviceState : onDeviceDisconnect(tenantId, deviceId, now)
  DeviceState -> StateStore : async save lastDisconnectTime
  DeviceState -> RuleQueue : DISCONNECT_EVENT
  note over DeviceState
    Disconnect does not force active=false.
    Activity status waits for its own timeout.
  end note
end

== SYNC request timeout ==
Device -> Protocol : one-shot GET Attributes or client RPC
Protocol -> Transport : registerSyncSession(sessionInfo, listener, timeout)
Transport -> LocalState : sessions.putIfAbsent and schedule future
Protocol -> Transport : process one-shot request
alt notification arrives first
  NotifyQueue -> Transport : ToTransportMsg(sessionId)
  Transport -> Protocol : listener callback
  Transport -> LocalState : auto deregister SYNC session and cancel future
  Protocol --> Device : response
else local timer fires first
  LocalState -> Protocol : onRemoteSessionCloseCommand("session timeout!")
  LocalState -> Transport : deregisterSession(sessionInfo)
  Protocol --> Device : protocol timeout response
  note over Transport,CoreQueue
    Timeout does not cancel a Core Queue record or continuing Actor work.
    A late notification is ignored because the listener is gone.
  end note
end

== Session inactivity protection ==
... no uplink for transport.sessions.inactivity_timeout ...
Transport -> LocalState : reporting-period expiry scan
LocalState -> Transport : session expired
Transport -> Transport : deregisterSession(sessionInfo)
Transport -> CoreQueue : ASYNC CLOSED
Transport -> Protocol : remote close command
Protocol --> Device : close socket or relation

... AppActor broadcasts SessionTimeoutCheckMsg every report period ...
ParentActors -> DeviceActor : checkSessionsTimeout()
DeviceActor -> DeviceActor : remove Actor sessions older than threshold
DeviceActor -> NotifyQueue : close notification to original nodeId
DeviceActor -> SessionCache : dump remaining snapshot
note over DeviceActor,DeviceState
  Actor-side timeout is defensive cleanup.
  It does not call onDeviceDisconnect and does not write lastDisconnectTime.
end note

== Device inactivity scheduler ==
... fixed-delay state scan, default 60 seconds ...
DeviceState -> DeviceState : checkStates() on owned Core partitions
DeviceState -> DeviceState : now >= lastActivityTime + inactivityTimeout
alt not already alarmed for this activity window
  DeviceState -> StateStore : async save inactivityAlarmTime=now
  DeviceState -> StateStore : async save active=false
  DeviceState -> RuleQueue : INACTIVITY_EVENT
  RuleQueue -> RuleChain : consume later
else already inactive or too new
  DeviceState -> DeviceState : no state transition
end

== Restart and routing ==
note over LocalState,SessionCache
  Transport restart always loses protocol listeners and activity states.
  Core restart skips restore for default Caffeine cache.
  Redis can restore Actor ASYNC metadata, not the network connection.
end note
DeviceActor -> SessionCache : restoreSessions() only for non-local cache
SessionCache --> DeviceActor : nodeId, sessionId, last activity and subscriptions
DeviceState -> StateStore : fetch six persistent keys on partition acquisition
StateStore --> DeviceState : persisted snapshot
DeviceState -> DeviceState : checkAndUpdateState using current wall clock

@enduml
